div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading it right now, it seems to be adressing, among other things, the possibility of the soul of the victim of <i>diablerie</i> to exerct influence on the diablerist, like a previous system to the one we find in V20 Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, but still no real system for the so called euphoria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T23:34:04-07:00","id":1543843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543770-on-the-euphoria-of-the-diablerie?p=1543837#post1543837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm reading it right now, it seems to be adressing, among other things, the possibility of the soul of the victim of <i>diablerie</i> to exerct influence on the diablerist, like a previous system to the one we find in V20 Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, but still no real system for the so called euphoria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it some more, are you sure you aren't conflating the mechanics for drinking Fae blood with Diablerie ? In <b>Vampire Dark Ages pg 262</b> there's a write up blerb about that.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the only things I can think of is pe